<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TestCaseEntity>
   <description>Summary: Shikhar App Requirement
Description: The Shikhar app must let users proceed through login with a mobile number. The login flow must display the country code and mobile-number prompt, allow the country code to be set to *+91*, and accept a mobile number. When the user taps *Login*, a number accepted for login must take the user to the PIN page. The user can then enter a six-digit PIN and submit it. If login is rejected, the app must display a clear invalid-login error without spelling mistakes.

Acceptance criteria

# The login screen displays a country-code selector and a mobile-number prompt.
# The user can select *+91* as the country code.
# The user can enter a mobile number and tap *Login*.
# For a number accepted by the login flow, the app displays the PIN page.
# If the PIN page appears while processing a dataset, remaining mobile-number entries are skipped.
# The user can enter a six-digit PIN and tap *Login*.
# If login is unsuccessful, the app displays an error message that clearly indicates the invalid-login condition and has no spelling errors.</description>
   <name>ORH5-13 Shikhar Login</name>
   <tag>regression,login</tag>
